     2	//!
     3	//! This implements the protocol semantics on top of the raw OSC capture:
     4	//! src/terminal/osc/parsers/kitty_clipboard_protocol.zig:
     5	//!
     6	//! The behavior here is modeled on the kitty reference implementation
     7	//! (kitty/clipboard.py) rather than only the prose spec, since the two
     8	//! disagree in places. Notable reference behaviors we reproduce:
     9	//!
    10	//!   * Malformed metadata (any record without '=', including an empty
    11	//!     metadata section) and an unknown or missing `type` silently drop
    12	//!     the request with no response.
    13	//!   * All base64 (payloads and the `mime`, `name`, and `pw` metadata
    14	//!     values) is strict RFC 4648 per the spec's "Encoding of payloads"
    15	//!     section: characters outside the standard alphabet (including
    16	//!     whitespace) and incorrect padding are rejected, never silently
    17	//!     skipped. An invalid value on `wdata` or `walias` aborts an
    18	//!     in-flight write with EINVAL; an invalid `read` is dropped with
    19	//!     no response since reads have no error status.
    20	//!   * Decoded metadata and MIME-list payloads must be valid UTF-8. An
    21	//!     invalid value on `wdata` or `walias`, or a `walias` without a
    22	//!     target MIME type, aborts an in-flight write with EINVAL.
    23	//!   * The `wdata` payloads for one MIME type form a single base64
    24	//!     stream split at arbitrary packet boundaries; only the
    25	//!     concatenation must be correctly padded. Like kitty (which
    26	//!     resets its streaming decoder on EOF), a packet ending exactly
    27	//!     at terminal padding restarts the stream, so independently
    28	//!     encoded chunks also work.
    29	//!   * `mime`, `name`, and `pw` metadata values are base64-encoded UTF-8;
    30	//!     everything else is verbatim. Unknown keys are ignored.
    31	//!   * `id` is sanitized by stripping characters outside [a-zA-Z0-9-_+.]
    32	//!     and truncating to 512 bytes, then echoed verbatim in every
    33	//!     response packet (omitted when empty).
    34	//!   * A `type=write` silently replaces any in-flight transaction. A
    35	//!     commit (`type=wdata` without a MIME type) with no in-flight
    36	//!     transaction is silently ignored.
    37	//!   * Responses never send a payload section for an empty payload,
    38	//!     except the targets ('.') listing DATA packet which is always sent.
    39	//!
    40	//! Specification: https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/clipboard/
    41	
